- The phase directive (the overseer, 2026-11-19): scope as the entry and its carries at `afa8699c`, nothing wider;
  P3 to say the row, the stamp's shape, the send reading and the split, then stop with one block in
  `founder-forks.md` before P4 (inputs#I1).

- **Answers it plans on:** `inputs#I2` (the founder's own words F1, F3, F4/F6, F5 and the overseer's technical
  answers F2 and items 6-11), on the block in `.andromeda/runs/2026-11-19T19-12-52Z-phase/founder-forks.md`;
  `inputs#I1` (the phase directive).

5. In `framing_turns`, right after the echo paste's block and inside the same `echo_from` arm (the transcript was read
   for the echo paste), add the `/context` paste:
   - the box guard first;
   - the prompt count read;
   - one `run.paste_text(PROBE_CONTEXT_COMMAND)`;
   - wait up to `probe_until` for `tags_since(&transcript, from_context) >= 1` or one more UserPromptSubmit, where
     `from_context` is `echo::end_of` read right before this paste (never the echo paste's offset, whose tag would
     count);
   - its ms recorded into the new `context` out-slot only for a tag with no prompt;
   - then `run.box_wait`.

   With no readable transcript, neither paste is typed and the row reads `fail`. A failed wait ends the turns as every
   earlier one does. The doc comment on `framing_turns` names the eighth paste.

8. Unit cases in `classify.rs` beside the echo cases (keeps tests S1):
   - `/context` on a verified CLI is confirmed by one new tag;
   - `/context` on an unverified CLI is `unconfirmable`;
   - `/context` whose remembered transcript path does NOT exist on disk is `unconfirmable` at once. This is F2's
     documented first-act reading (the `echoed` helper, with the transcript removed before the send).

10. Move every relied-row count pin from 24 to 25, appending `local-command-context` last wherever a list of ids is
    pinned:
    - `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/ledger/test_cases*.rs` (the `ALL` order, the stamp of exactly 24 ids now reading
      unverified, and 25 reading verified);
    - `src/run/version_gate.rs` (the stamps-verdict ladder gains one push);
    - `crates/viola-e2e/src/harness/run.rs` (`LEDGER_ROWS` and its verify-stdout pin);
    - `tests/cli_verify.rs` (the all-pass stdout and `STAMPED_PASS`);
    - `tests/cli_verify/runs.rs` (the local-command row cases);
    - `tests/support/verify.rs` and `tests/support/home.rs` (the stamped home);
    - `tests/contract_ledger_probes.rs` (`ROW_IDS` and the `stamped … 25 pass  0 fail` line);
    - `tests/contract_fixture_hygiene.rs` and `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/screen.rs`. Each hit is read first at
      implement, and only a hit that IS the relied-row count moves.

    The sweep pattern is testing.md 2026-10-14's retired-shape probe (`/24\]`, `[&str; 24]`, `24 pass  0 fail`), run
    again before the first gate, with every caller of a moved shared helper's count in the gate filter (testing.md
    2026-10-07).

17. `rig_rehearsal_cs_keeps_the_stamp_and_reads_the_config_top_level` over the fake:
    - `verify-exit: 0`, `local-command-context: pass`, `pass-count: 25/25`, `kept-stamp: written`;
    - a `config-top:` line present, holding no `/`;
    - a second `cs` in the same out dir reads `kept-stamp: exists`, the first file unchanged by sha;
    - the teardown words.

21. Rig inline cases:
    - the four labels' arms;
    - `send_word`'s two `ok` shapes;
    - `config-top`'s name rule (a plain name, `other`, never deeper);
    - the hint-cell reader over a fed vt100 screen (cells 2..N, attribute words only), with literals copied from what
      was fed (testing.md 2026-11-13);
    - `FLOOR_ROWS`'s doc pin.

22. Fired through `gate.py run --live-legs`, in block order:
    - the install read by path;
    - the census;
    - the plain build and hash;
    - the host read;
    - the scratch base read;
    - the kept stamp's absence;
    - the live home stamps' sha (before);
    - `CS`;
    - the census, the live home sha (unmoved), the kept stamp present;
    - `CC`;
    - then the spare's two conditional entries;
    - then the operator-keyed census and sha after the last leg.

    One ledger file, `--cap 2 --spare 1`. The spare (`CS-2` or `CC-2`, one of them at most) is fired only for a start
    stopped BEFORE its reading by the host, the token window (uncounted: stop and say so) or the rig's own refusal,
    never on a red reading (`inputs#I2` item 3). Unfired, it is recorded `not fired — spare unspent`.

- (live, `CC`) under the kept stamp:
  - `send-2-reply: ok`, `context-submitted: no`, a tag count of at least 1;
  - the hint words recorded as readings;
  - the teardown words.

22. Fired through `gate.py run --live-legs`, in block order:
    - the install read by path;
    - the census;
    - the plain build and hash;
    - the host read;
    - the scratch base read;
    - the kept stamp's absence;
    - the live home stamps' sha (before);
    - `CS`;
    - the census, the live home sha (unmoved), the kept stamp present;
    - `CC`;
    - then the spare's two conditional entries;
    - then the operator-keyed census and sha after the last leg.

    One ledger file. `--cap` is the RUNNING total of base starts in that file: `CS` and `CS-2` take `--cap 1`, `CC`
    and `CC-2` take `--cap 2`, every start `--spare 1`. With `--cap 2` on `CS`, a second `CS` would be admitted.

    The host is read before EACH start, not only before `CS`. The host-read entry (the `hostwatch.py read --last 15`
    entry ahead of `CS`) is fired again by `--entry` right before `CC` and right before a spare. Each reading is
    recorded: QUIET fires; CONTENDED with a NEIGHBOUR named stops and is re-read, never retried into.

    The spare (`CS-2` or `CC-2`, one of them at most) is fired only for a start
    stopped BEFORE its reading by the host, the token window (uncounted: stop and say so) or the rig's own refusal,
    never on a red reading (`inputs#I2` item 3). Unfired, it is recorded `not fired — spare unspent`.

